--- !u!114 &1290509813841232599
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4096943794514430410}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 20ed5253628c2b64ca7097d0235ae44e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  imageRoot: {fileID: 4326090657816020604}
  titleTMPText: {fileID: 351832941626899494}
  contentTMPText: {fileID: 6742802357242262530}
  scoreTMPText: {fileID: 2249296978571599}
  scoreFormat: '{0:0}'
  endings:
  - index: 0
    imageObject: {fileID: 2801163128566983484}
    title: Beyond English
    content: You study hard and received the most red flowers in the class. Teacher
      Julian invited you to do an interview with him, saying you've already gone beyond
      English.
  - index: 1
    imageObject: {fileID: 4205103347847168706}
    title: Go West
    content: You have understood the essence of English all by teaching yourself
      on the internet. You have never left Y City, yet your pronunciation is standard.
      Julian says don't waste your talent. This blessing is almost like a curse.
      In every choice you make later in life, it asks you to go out, and not to
      stop.
  - index: 2
    imageObject: {fileID: 7595621942585135166}
    title: Touching Effort
    content: You finish every exercise, memorize every word, and copy every mistake
      again in three different colors. Julian says your problem is not attitude,
      but method. You nod. Somehow, this hurts more than criticism.
  - index: 3
    imageObject: {fileID: 362279778671449139}
    title: It's fine to be bad at English.
    content: Contrary to Julian's imagination, about 6.77 billion people in the
      world do not use English, accounting for 81.6% of the global population. You
      never go beyond English, nor beyond yourself. You simply grow up and forget
      many words in an ordinary way. It's fine to be bad at English. We love our
      country.
  - index: 4
    imageObject: {fileID: 3141347947787667605}
    title: The Things That Last
    content: Three days after the exam, you forgot what you had studied for three
      years. April is over, April is over. There are all kinds of love in the world,
      but never the same love twice.
  - index: 5
    imageObject: {fileID: 1779022591729426259}
    title: Separate Ways
    content: You never made a solemn farewell. It was just that later, she went
      to a new school, and you went to your own class. Both of you felt that this
      did not count as losing each other. Until one day, you remembered something
      that only she would laugh at, but no longer knew who to share it with.
  autoCollectImagesOnAwake: 1
  showEndingOnStart: 0
  startEndingIndex: 0
